			],
			"Message": "style(Mountain): Clean up formatting across ApplicationState modules and command handlers\n\nApply consistent formatting improvements across Mountain's application state hierarchy, command registration, document save operations, workspace provider, extension scanner, and shutdown logic:\n\n- Convert multi-line `use std::{...}` imports to single-line format across 20+ state modules (ConfigurationState, ExtensionRegistry, ProviderRegistration, ScannedExtensions, DebugState, DecorationsState, DiagnosticsState, DocumentState, KeybindingState, LifecyclePhaseState, MarkerState, NavigationHistoryState, OutputChannelState, TreeViewState, WebviewState, WorkingCopyState, UIState, WorkspaceState)\n- Condense single-statement getter methods to single-line format (GetAll, Get, Count, Contains variants)\n- Normalize lock acquisition patterns: remove extra blank lines around `.lock()` calls, standardize guard binding\n- Fix indentation in AppLifecycle (GlobalMementoPath setup), Entry (dev_log call), Bootstrap command registration, FileExplorerViewProvider\n- Simplify SCM command handlers (GetAllSourceControlManagementState, GetSCMResourceChanges) by inlining lock/clone chains\n- Clean up DocumentProvider save operations: flatten nested lock access paths\n- Fix WorkspaceProvider walk loop indentation (break/quit conditions)\n- Update ExtensionManagement scanner and default configs: flatten Extensions lock access\n- Add missing newlines at end of files (ApplicationState.rs, ConfigurationState.rs, ExtensionRegistry.rs, ProviderRegistration.rs, ScannedExtensions.rs, DebugState.rs, DecorationsState.rs, DiagnosticsState.rs, DocumentState.rs, KeybindingState.rs, LifecyclePhaseState.rs, MarkerState.rs, NavigationHistoryState.rs, OutputChannelState.rs, TreeViewState.rs, WebviewState.rs, WorkingCopyState.rs, UIState.rs, WorkspaceState.rs, SaveApplicationState.rs, VineHostImpl.rs)\n- Fix shell integration script: add space in `2> /dev/null` redirection\n\nNo functional changes — purely mechanical formatting cleanup for consistency across Mountain's state management layer and related command handlers.",
			"SHA": "a94d949e10d5ba5d46a408ff3c7ef99d2dc6f684"
		}
